(7684849, 1257917, 30214, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Bear_Music:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by glad2badad:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LevT:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats, Barry! ...Incidentally, I''m about to pull the trigger on Mavic Air 2. Seems like it can be a ribbon-getter )) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>The FCC states that there is a limit of 5 owners per any internet photo contest site.  I think Paul snuck in before the final rule was written.  Sorry Lev, but you''re going to have to find something else to spend your money on.  :-D   I wonder if Robert is thinking the same.  LOL </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Absolutely. The skies are getting too crowded in DPCland. Here''s an idea for you: get one of those SUBMERSIBLE drones and show us deepscapes :-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Sorry guys, too late now, I am a member of your club whether you like it or not! On the other hand, I do like to fly over the ocean (at least, I did it a number of times with my Mavic Mini), so there is always a chance that my spanking new drone will become if not submerSIBLE, then at least submerGED (I hope not!).<br/> <br/>I took my new Air 2 up for a spin first time today, and I must say I am really impressed. Stable as a rock in pretty windy conditions. Seamless connection at all times (I flew it up to about 600m away). My Mini would be whining, refusing to follow commands, losing connection, and trying to land. Did not look at the photos and videos yet.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2021-01-19 01:12:15.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Bear_Music: Originally posted by glad2badad: Originally posted by LevT: Congrats, Barry! ...Incidentally, I''m about to pull the trigger on Mavic Air 2. Seems like it can be a ribbon-getter ))  The FCC states that there is a limit of 5 owners per any internet photo contest site.  I think Paul snuck in before the final rule was written.  Sorry Lev, but you''re going to have to find something else to spend your money on.  :-D   I wonder if Robert is thinking the same.  LOL  Absolutely. The skies are getting too crowded in DPCland. Here''s an idea for you: get one of those SUBMERSIBLE drones and show us deepscapes :-)  Sorry guys, too late now, I am a member of your club whether you like it or not! On the other hand, I do like to fly over the ocean (at least, I did it a number of times with my Mavic Mini), so there is always a chance that my spanking new drone will become if not submerSIBLE, then at least submerGED (I hope not!). I took my new Air 2 up for a spin first time today, and I must say I am really impressed. Stable as a rock in pretty windy conditions. Seamless connection at all times (I flew it up to about 600m away). My Mini would be whining, refusing to follow commands, losing connection, and trying to land. Did not look at the photos and videos yet.', '2021-01-18 23:24:40.000000', '2021-01-19 01:12:15.000000', 0),
(7701848, 1257929, 30049, '<td valign="top">Ahhh ... yes, I see the gains made with this shot of yours in comparison.  Cool!<br/> <br/><a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1264235" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/3000-3999/3274/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1264235.jpg" xalt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/3000-3999/3274/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1264235.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/3000-3999/3274/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1264235.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/></a></td>', 'Ahhh ... yes, I see the gains made with this shot of yours in comparison.  Cool! ', '2021-09-22 21:35:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(7701850, 1257929, 60581, '<td valign="top">Agreed and yes, this is a real improvement! Very well captured shot Gina!<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by glad2badad:</b></div><hr/><i> Ahhh ... yes, I see the gains made with this shot of yours in comparison.  Cool!<br/> <br/><a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1264235" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/3000-3999/3274/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1264235.jpg" xalt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/3000-3999/3274/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1264235.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/3000-3999/3274/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1264235.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/></a> </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Agreed and yes, this is a real improvement! Very well captured shot Gina! Originally posted by glad2badad: Ahhh ... yes, I see the gains made with this shot of yours in comparison.  Cool!  ', '2021-09-22 21:40:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(7701862, 1257929, 67145, '<td valign="top">and ''some'' say its not about the equipment ... <br/>just seeing the difference between these two images .. the one for the new years resolution and the extended free study .. makes it so obvious that you were hindered in your ability to capture the shots you visualized by the equipment you were using .. <br/>having said that . <br/>some ppl have the most amazing equipment but still take photos that arent that good .. <br/>but if you have a talent . which you obviously have .. it can be a wonderful experience to get a camera that performs to your creativity .. its like a whole new world opens up .. <br/>thats what happened for me when i got my first macro lens ...  <br/>i''m so glad i just happened to see your thread <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1415010" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">its all about the camera and the lens</a> ..</td>', 'and ''some'' say its not about the equipment ... just seeing the difference between these two images .. the one for the new years resolution and the extended free study .. makes it so obvious that you were hindered in your ability to capture the shots you visualized by the equipment you were using .. having said that . some ppl have the most amazing equipment but still take photos that arent that good .. but if you have a talent . which you obviously have .. it can be a wonderful experience to get a camera that performs to your creativity .. its like a whole new world opens up .. thats what happened for me when i got my first macro lens ...  i''m so glad i just happened to see your thread its all about the camera and the lens ..', '2021-09-23 01:04:48.000000', NULL, 0),
